-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

In-tree third-party source adaptations:

* Arm Optimized Routines:
  src/merlin/runtime/portable_exp.c, portable_pow.c, and portable_trig.c.
  MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception. See
  src/merlin/runtime/portable_trig.LICENSE and portable_math.provenance.json
  for the preserved license, source revision, and file provenance.

* OpenLibm / FDLIBM:
  src/merlin/runtime/portable_tanh.c.
  Sun permission notices are retained in the adapted source. See
  src/merlin/runtime/portable_tanh.LICENSE and portable_math.provenance.json.

* LLVM MLIR TextMate grammar:
  build_tools/plots/snippet2svg/grammar.json.
  Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception. See the adjacent UPSTREAM.md and
  LICENSE.llvm.txt for source identity and license text.

* Optional Atlas LSTMNetViT model loader:
  merlin/contract/capsules/atlas/model/M1_lstmnetvit_atlas/capsule.loader_deps/.
  Copyright (c) 2024 Anish Bhattacharya, Nishanth Rao, and Dhruv Parikh.
  Its adjacent LICENSE is titled "MIT License with Commercial Use
  Restriction" and prohibits commercial use without prior permission.
  This component is not offered under Merlin's Apache license.

Git submodules:

The source tree records LLVM/MLIR at third_party/llvm-project. That external
repository retains its own license and notices. External compiler baselines
and optional toolchains are not licensed by this NOTICE.

Separate evaluation artifacts:

Historical test/runtime sources, toolchain installations, external expert
implementations, and generated evaluation binaries are separate artifacts.
Their own license and attribution records apply. In particular, the
preserved Gemmini test root and riscv-tests have BSD notices, while
rocc-software has Apache-2.0 terms. These artifacts are not vendored at the
former harness_curated path.

